/T (Switch Bioworks, established in 2022 and headquartered in San Carlos, CA, is a biotechnology company spun out of Stanford University. The company specializes in engineering microbes using advanced synthetic biology to produce sustainable nitrogen fertilizers. By harnessing innovative gene editing techniques and metabolic engineering, Switch Bioworks creates living fertilizers that enable plants to access nitrogen more efficiently, reducing the dependence on traditional chemical fertilizers. The company's technology represents a breakthrough in sustainable agriculture, contributing to both environmental sustainability and agricultural productivity.)
